## Secure Implementation

### Tier 1: Critical Fix (5 minutes)
**Objective**: Immediately block unauthenticated access to admin and actuator endpoints

**What This Tier Addresses:**
- Prevents anonymous access to sensitive endpoints
- Re-enables CSRF protection for state-changing requests
- Restricts actuator exposure to health checks only

**Implementation:**

```java
package com.example.security;

import org.springframework.context.annotation.Bean;
import org.springframework.context.annotation.Configuration;
import org.springframework.security.config.annotation.web.builders.HttpSecurity;
import org.springframework.security.web.SecurityFilterChain;
import org.springframework.boot.actuate.autoconfigure.security.servlet.EndpointRequest;

/**
 * TIER 1 SECURE: Basic authentication and actuator protection
 * 
 * Defenses:
 * - Require authentication for /admin/** and actuator endpoints
 * - CSRF protection enabled (Spring Security default)
 * - Limit actuator exposure to health and info only
 * 
 * Time to implement: 5 minutes
 * Prevents: Anonymous access, credential harvesting from /actuator/env
 */
@Configuration
public class Tier1SecurityConfig {

    @Bean
    public SecurityFilterChain filterChain(HttpSecurity http) throws Exception {
        http
            .authorizeHttpRequests(authorize -> authorize
                .requestMatchers("/actuator/health", "/actuator/info").permitAll()  // Public health checks
                .requestMatchers("/actuator/**").authenticated()                    // Secure all other actuator endpoints
                .requestMatchers("/admin/**").authenticated()                       // Require auth for admin
                .anyRequest().permitAll()                                          // Allow public API access
            )
            .httpBasic(basic -> {})  // Enable HTTP Basic authentication
            // CSRF enabled by default - do NOT disable unless using stateless JWT
            .headers(headers -> headers
                .frameOptions(frame -> frame.deny())  // Prevent clickjacking
            );

        return http.build();
    }
}

/**
 * application-prod.yml:
 * 
 * management:
 *   endpoints:
 *     web:
 *       exposure:
 *         include: health,info    # Only expose safe endpoints
 *   endpoint:
 *     health:
 *       show-details: when-authorized  # Require auth for detailed health info
 */
```

**Limitations:**
- Still allows any authenticated user to access /admin endpoints (no role enforcement)
- HTTP Basic auth sends credentials with every request (less secure than token-based)
- No audit logging of administrative actions
- No rate limiting on sensitive endpoints

