### Tier 2: Essential Defenses (15 minutes)
**Objective**: Implement role-based access control and method-level security

**What This Tier Adds:**
- Role-based authorization (only ADMIN users can access admin endpoints)
- Method-level security annotations for fine-grained control
- Actuator endpoints selectively exposed based on sensitivity
- JWT-based authentication (stateless, more scalable than sessions)

**Implementation:**

```java
package com.example.security;

import org.springframework.context.annotation.Bean;
import org.springframework.context.annotation.Configuration;
import org.springframework.security.config.annotation.method.configuration.EnableMethodSecurity;
import org.springframework.security.config.annotation.web.builders.HttpSecurity;
import org.springframework.security.config.http.SessionCreationPolicy;
import org.springframework.security.web.SecurityFilterChain;
import org.springframework.security.web.authentication.UsernamePasswordAuthenticationFilter;
import org.springframework.boot.actuate.autoconfigure.security.servlet.EndpointRequest;

/**
 * TIER 2 SECURE: Role-based access control with JWT authentication
 * 
 * Defenses:
 * - ADMIN role required for /admin/** endpoints
 * - Method-level security with @PreAuthorize annotations
 * - JWT authentication (stateless, suitable for APIs)
 * - Selective actuator endpoint exposure
 * - CSRF can be safely disabled (stateless JWT, no cookies)
 * 
 * Time to implement: 15 minutes
 * Prevents: Privilege escalation, unauthorized admin actions, session-based attacks
 */
@Configuration
@EnableMethodSecurity(prePostEnabled = true)  // Enables @PreAuthorize annotations
public class Tier2SecurityConfig {

    @Autowired
    private JwtAuthenticationFilter jwtAuthFilter;

    @Bean
    public SecurityFilterChain filterChain(HttpSecurity http) throws Exception {
        http
            .authorizeHttpRequests(authorize -> authorize
                // Public endpoints
                .requestMatchers("/api/public/**", "/actuator/health").permitAll()

                // Actuator endpoints require ADMIN role
                .requestMatchers("/actuator/**").hasRole("ADMIN")

                // Admin endpoints require ADMIN role
                .requestMatchers("/admin/**").hasRole("ADMIN")

                // All other endpoints require authentication (any role)
                .anyRequest().authenticated()
            )
            // Stateless session (JWT-based, no server-side sessions)
            .sessionManagement(session -> session
                .sessionCreationPolicy(SessionCreationPolicy.STATELESS)
            )
            // CSRF can be disabled for stateless JWT (no cookies)
            .csrf(csrf -> csrf.disable())
            // Add JWT filter before UsernamePasswordAuthenticationFilter
            .addFilterBefore(jwtAuthFilter, UsernamePasswordAuthenticationFilter.class)
            .headers(headers -> headers
                .frameOptions(frame -> frame.deny())
            );

        return http.build();
    }
}

/**
 * Admin controller with method-level security
 */
@RestController
@RequestMapping("/admin")
class SecureAdminController {

    @Autowired
    private UserRepository userRepository;

    @Autowired
    private AuditLogger auditLogger;

    /**
     * SECURE: Requires ADMIN role, validates input, logs action
     */
    @PostMapping("/users/{id}/promote")
    @PreAuthorize("hasRole('ADMIN')")  // Redundant with SecurityFilterChain but defense-in-depth
    public ResponseEntity<?> promoteUser(
        @PathVariable Long id,
        @AuthenticationPrincipal UserDetails admin
    ) {
        // Validate user exists
        User user = userRepository.findById(id)
            .orElseThrow(() -> new ResourceNotFoundException("User not found"));

        // Prevent self-promotion (business logic)
        if (user.getUsername().equals(admin.getUsername())) {
            throw new IllegalOperationException("Cannot promote yourself");
        }

        // Update role
        String previousRole = user.getRole();
        user.setRole("ADMIN");
        userRepository.save(user);

        // Audit log
        auditLogger.log(AuditEvent.builder()
            .action("USER_PROMOTED")
            .actor(admin.getUsername())
            .target(user.getUsername())
            .details(Map.of("previousRole", previousRole, "newRole", "ADMIN"))
            .timestamp(Instant.now())
            .build());

        return ResponseEntity.ok(Map.of(
            "status", "success",
            "userId", id,
            "newRole", "ADMIN"
        ));
    }

    /**
     * SECURE: Requires ADMIN role, paginates results, excludes sensitive fields
     */
    @GetMapping("/users")
    @PreAuthorize("hasRole('ADMIN')")
    public Page<UserDTO> getAllUsers(Pageable pageable) {
        return userRepository.findAll(pageable)
            .map(user -> new UserDTO(user));  // DTO excludes password hash, SSN
    }
}

/**
 * application-prod.yml:
 * 
 * management:
 *   endpoints:
 *     web:
 *       exposure:
 *         include: health,info,metrics,prometheus  # Selective exposure
 *   endpoint:
 *     health:
 *       show-details: when-authorized  # Require ADMIN for details
 *   security:
 *     enabled: true
 *     roles: ADMIN  # Only ADMIN role can access actuator
 */
```

**Improvements Over Tier 1:**
- JWT-based authentication (no session state, better scalability)
- Role-based authorization (only ADMIN users access admin endpoints)
- Method-level security annotations (defense-in-depth)
- Audit logging of sensitive operations
- Input validation and business logic checks
- DTO pattern prevents accidental PII exposure

**Remaining Limitations:**
- No network segmentation (actuator still accessible from public internet)
- No rate limiting (vulnerable to brute force)
- Secrets still in environment variables (visible in /actuator/env to authenticated ADMIN)
- No intrusion detection or anomaly detection

