## Monitoring & Alerting

### Prometheus Metrics for Security Monitoring

```yaml
# prometheus-metrics.yml
# Security-specific metrics for detecting attacks

metrics:
  - name: security_filter_denials_total
    type: counter
    description: "Total requests denied by security filters"
    labels: [endpoint, reason]
    alert_threshold: 10 per minute
    alert_severity: warning

  - name: unauthorized_admin_access_attempts_total
    type: counter
    description: "Unauthenticated attempts to access /admin endpoints"
    labels: [endpoint, source_ip]
    alert_threshold: 5 per minute
    alert_severity: high
    alert_action: "Block IP at firewall after 20 attempts"

  - name: actuator_env_access_total
    type: counter
    description: "Access attempts to /actuator/env endpoint"
    labels: [authenticated, source_ip]
    alert_threshold: 1 per hour
    alert_severity: critical
    rationale: "This endpoint should rarely be accessed; any access may indicate reconnaissance"

  - name: csrf_token_validation_failures_total
    type: counter
    description: "CSRF token validation failures"
    labels: [endpoint]
    alert_threshold: 10 per minute
    alert_severity: warning

  - name: user_privilege_escalation_attempts_total
    type: counter
    description: "Attempts to promote users to admin role"
    labels: [actor, target_user]
    alert_threshold: 5 per hour
    alert_severity: critical
    alert_action: "Freeze actor account, page security team"
```

### Alert Rules (Prometheus Alertmanager)

```yaml
groups:
  - name: security_alerts
    interval: 30s
    rules:
      # CRITICAL: Actuator endpoint accessed from non-VPC IP
      - alert: ActuatorAccessFromPublicIP
        expr: rate(security_actuator_access_denied_total[5m]) > 0
        for: 1m
        labels:
          severity: critical
        annotations:
          summary: "Actuator access attempt from public IP detected"
          description: "IP {{ $labels.ip }} attempted to access {{ $labels.endpoint }}. This should be impossible if network segmentation is correct."
          remediation: "1. Verify firewall rules restrict port 9090 to VPC CIDR. 2. Check for VPN compromise. 3. Review security group changes."

      # HIGH: Multiple failed authentication attempts (potential brute force)
      - alert: BruteForceAttackDetected
        expr: rate(security_authentication_failures_total[2m]) > 5
        for: 5m
        labels:
          severity: high
        annotations:
          summary: "Potential brute force attack detected"
          description: "{{ $value }} authentication failures per second from {{ $labels.source_ip }}"
          remediation: "1. Block IP at WAF. 2. Review authentication logs. 3. Check for credential stuffing."

      # CRITICAL: Privilege escalation attempt
      - alert: PrivilegeEscalationAttempt
        expr: rate(security_privilege_escalation_attempts_total[5m]) > 0
        for: 1m
        labels:
          severity: critical
        annotations:
          summary: "Privilege escalation attempt detected"
          description: "User {{ $labels.actor }} attempted to promote {{ $labels.target_user }} to ADMIN role"
          remediation: "1. Freeze actor account immediately. 2. Review actor's recent actions in audit log. 3. Page security team."
