## Configuration Management: Development vs. Production

### Environment-Specific Configuration Pattern

**application-dev.yml (Local Development)**
```yaml
spring:
  security:
    user:
      name: dev
      password: dev  # Acceptable for local only

management:
  endpoints:
    web:
      exposure:
        include: "*"  # All endpoints for debugging
  endpoint:
    health:
      show-details: always

logging:
  level:
    org.springframework.security: DEBUG  # Verbose security logs
```

**application-prod.yml (Production)**
```yaml
spring:
  security:
    # No default user, JWT authentication required

management:
  server:
    port: 9090  # Separate port, firewalled
  endpoints:
    web:
      exposure:
        include: health,info,metrics,prometheus  # Selective
  endpoint:
    health:
      show-details: when-authorized  # Require auth for details

logging:
  level:
    org.springframework.security: INFO  # Production-appropriate logging
```

**Profile-Specific Security Configuration**
```java
@Configuration
@Profile("dev")
class DevSecurityConfig {
    @Bean
    public SecurityFilterChain devFilterChain(HttpSecurity http) throws Exception {
        // Permissive for local development
        return http
            .authorizeHttpRequests(auth -> auth.anyRequest().permitAll())
            .csrf(csrf -> csrf.disable())
            .build();
    }
}

@Configuration
@Profile("prod")
class ProdSecurityConfig {
    @Bean
    public SecurityFilterChain prodFilterChain(HttpSecurity http) throws Exception {
        // Hardened for production (see Tier 3 above)
        return http
            .authorizeHttpRequests(auth -> auth
                .requestMatchers("/admin/**").hasRole("ADMIN")
                .anyRequest().authenticated()
            )
            .build();
    }
}
```

**Activation**
```bash
# Local development
export SPRING_PROFILES_ACTIVE=dev
java -jar app.jar

# Production
export SPRING_PROFILES_ACTIVE=prod
java -jar app.jar
```

**CI/CD Pipeline Enforcement**
```yaml
# .github/workflows/deploy.yml
jobs:
  deploy:
    steps:
      - name: Verify production profile
        run: |
          if grep -q "permitAll()" src/main/java/com/example/security/*SecurityConfig.java; then
            echo "ERROR: permitAll() found in SecurityConfig"
            exit 1
          fi

      - name: Verify actuator exposure
        run: |
          if grep -q 'include: "\*"' src/main/resources/application-prod.yml; then
            echo "ERROR: All actuator endpoints exposed in prod config"
            exit 1
          fi
```

This ensures development shortcuts cannot accidentally reach production.
